{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>believeth every word</b> — to turn aside from the straight path." "<b>and the prudent understandeth</b> — on account of his proper prudence. And the meaning: his way, from which he does not turn aside; therefore the wise fear is after him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "אשורו could also point to 'his step' (from אשר); rendered 'his prudence' following the immediate lexical link to ערום. The last clause על כן אחריו חכם ירא is obscure and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:45.139631529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}